---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
<Fragment slot="head">
<meta name="description" content="The free business in a box checklist: seven things a small business should own online, each with a free or cheap way to start and a five minute self-test. Every pick says whether I have used it.">
<title>Business in a Box: A Free Checklist to Own Your Business Online | BlueYucca</title>
<link rel="canonical" href="https://blueyucca.com/business-in-a-box">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="BlueYucca">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:title" content="Business in a Box: A Free Checklist to Own Your Business Online | BlueYucca">
<meta property="og:description" content="Seven things a small business should own online, each with a free or cheap start and a five minute self-test.">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://blueyucca.com/business-in-a-box">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
<style is:inline>
  :root {
    --cream: #FAF6ED; --cream-deep: #F3ECDC; --card: #FFFDF8;
    --sand: #E5DAC3; --sand-dark: #D5C6A5;
    --ink: #1E2A45; --ink-soft: #52607E;
    --blue: #2455C4; --blue-deep: #17357F; --blue-dark: #1B3A8C;
    --blue-soft: #4B79DC; --blue-wash: #E9EFFB; --blue-line: #C9D8F5;
    --haz: #F2C94C;
    --mono: "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body {
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    background: var(--cream); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.65;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  ::selection { background: var(--blue); color: var(--cream); }
  a { color: var(--blue); }
  .wrap { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(22px); transition: opacity 0.6s ease, transform 0.6s ease; }
  .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
    html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
  }
  header.site {
    position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 50;
    background: rgba(250,246,237,0.88);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .nav { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 13px 24px; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .brand {
    font-weight: 900; font-size: 1.45rem; color: var(--blue-deep);
    text-decoration: none; letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    transform: rotate(-2deg); display: inline-block;
    text-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--sand); transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }
  .brand:hover { transform: rotate(1deg) scale(1.04); }
  .brand .b1 { color: var(--blue); } .brand .b2 { color: var(--ink); }
  .nav-links { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .nav-links a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .nav-links a:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  .nav-cta {
    background: var(--blue); color: var(--cream) !important;
    padding: 8px 16px; border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--ink); font-weight: 800 !important;
    transition: transform 0.1s ease, box-shadow 0.1s ease;
  }
  .nav-cta:hover { transform: translate(1px, 1px); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .nav-links { gap: 14px; font-size: 0.9rem; } }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700;
    background: var(--ink); color: var(--cream); padding: 4px 10px;
    transform: rotate(-1deg); margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .hero { padding: 72px 0 30px; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.4vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.02em; font-weight: 900; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .hero .lede { font-size: 1.18rem; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .btn-row { display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1rem;
    padding: 13px 22px; border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--ink);
    transition: transform 0.1s ease, box-shadow 0.1s ease;
  }
  .btn:hover { transform: translate(2px, 2px); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--ink); }
  .btn.primary { background: var(--blue); color: var(--cream); }
  .btn.secondary { background: var(--card); color: var(--ink); }


  .quick-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin: 40px 0 20px; }
  .quick {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--sand-dark);
    padding: 18px;
  }
  .quick strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .quick p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .quick:nth-child(odd) { transform: rotate(-0.4deg); }
  .quick:nth-child(even) { transform: rotate(0.4deg); }

  section.block { padding: 54px 0 10px; }
  .kicker { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.74rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue-deep); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  section.block h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.6vw, 2.3rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  section.block .sub { color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 26px; }

  .datechip {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
    background: var(--haz); color: var(--ink); border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 3px 9px; transform: rotate(-1deg); margin-left: 10px; vertical-align: middle;
  }

  .current-note {
    background: var(--blue-wash); border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--ink); padding: 24px 26px; margin: 44px 0 8px;
  }
  .current-note .kicker { color: var(--blue-deep); }
  .current-note p { color: var(--ink); max-width: 760px; }
  .current-note p + p { margin-top: 10px; }

  .compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 22px; margin-top: 10px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .col { border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 24px; background: var(--card); }
  .col.them { background: var(--cream-deep); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); }
  .col.us { background: var(--card); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--blue); }
  .col .tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .col.us .tag { color: var(--blue-deep); }
  .col h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .col ul { list-style: none; }
  .col li { padding: 7px 0 7px 26px; position: relative; font-size: 0.97rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .col.them li::before { content: "\2717"; position: absolute; left: 2px; color: #B0483C; font-weight: 700; }
  .col.us li::before { content: "\2713"; position: absolute; left: 2px; color: var(--blue); font-weight: 700; }

  .steps-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .step-card { background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); padding: 22px; }
  .step-num { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--blue-deep); letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .step-card h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 6px 0 8px; }
  .step-card p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .chipbar {
    margin-top: 14px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--ink); color: var(--cream); padding: 8px 10px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .chipbar .live { color: #7CFC9A; font-weight: 700; }

  .tool-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .tool-card { background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); padding: 22px; position: relative; }
  .tool-card.featured { box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--blue); }
  .tool-card h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .tool-card p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .tool-card .status {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue-deep);
  }
  .tool-card .go { font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; }
  .sticker {
    position: absolute; top: -12px; right: 12px;
    background: var(--haz); border: 2px solid var(--ink); font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; padding: 3px 8px;
    transform: rotate(3deg);
  }


  .post-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .post-card {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark);
    padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  }
  .post-card .pdate { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .post-card h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .post-card h3 a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }
  .post-card h3 a:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  .post-card p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); flex: 1; }
  .post-card .read { font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 12px; }

  .why { background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--blue); padding: 30px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .why p { max-width: 760px; color: var(--ink); }
  .why p + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  mark { background: var(--haz); padding: 1px 5px; }

  .stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .stat { border: 2px solid var(--ink); background: var(--card); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); padding: 22px; }
  .stat .big { font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 900; color: var(--blue-deep); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .stat strong { display: block; margin-top: 4px; }
  .stat p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  details {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--sand-dark); margin-bottom: 14px; padding: 0;
  }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 800; padding: 16px 20px; list-style: none; }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary::after { content: "+"; float: right; font-weight: 900; color: var(--blue); }
  details[open] summary::after { content: "\2212"; }
  details p { padding: 0 20px 18px; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: 28px; align-items: start; margin-top: 8px; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .about-main p { color: var(--ink); max-width: 640px; }
  .about-main p + p, .about-main h3 + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  .about-main h3 { margin-top: 22px; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .funfact {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark);
    padding: 22px; transform: rotate(0.6deg);
  }
  .funfact .tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-weight: 700; background: var(--haz); border: 2px solid var(--ink); display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .funfact h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .funfact p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .whois { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 12px; }

  .cta-final { text-align: center; padding: 70px 0 60px; }
  .cta-final h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin-bottom: 12px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .cta-final p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .cta-final .btn-row { justify-content: center; }

  .site-footer { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); background: var(--cream-deep); padding: 30px 0 40px; margin-top: 30px; text-align: center; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .site-footer nav { margin: 14px 0; }
  .site-footer a { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .site-footer a:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  .retro-badge {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; background: var(--ink); color: #7CFC9A;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 5px 12px; transform: rotate(-1deg);
  }
  .chip {
    display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 2px 8px;
    border: 2px solid var(--ink); color: var(--ink); vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .chip.used { background: var(--blue-wash); }
  .chip.testing { background: var(--haz); }
  .chip.nottested { background: var(--cream-deep); }
  .chip.mixed { background: var(--card); border-style: dashed; }
  .chip.cost { background: var(--ink); color: var(--cream); }

  .box-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 18px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .box-card {
    display: block; background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--sand-dark); padding: 20px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink);
    transition: transform 0.1s ease, box-shadow 0.1s ease;
  }
  .box-card:hover { transform: translate(2px, 2px); box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 var(--sand-dark); }
  .box-num { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--blue-deep); letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .box-card h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 6px 0 6px; }
  .box-card p { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 12px; }

  .legend { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-top: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .item {
    background: var(--card); border: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--sand-dark);
    padding: 26px; margin: 34px 0; scroll-margin-top: 90px;
  }
  .item-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .item-num { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--blue-deep); letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .item h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; }
  .item dl { margin-top: 8px; }
  .item dt {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 700; color: var(--blue-deep); margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .item dd { margin: 4px 0 0; max-width: 740px; }
  .selftest { background: var(--blue-wash); border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 14px 16px; }
  .pick { border-top: 2px dashed var(--sand-dark); margin-top: 12px; padding-top: 12px; }
  .pick:first-child { border-top: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
  .why .fine { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-family: var(--mono); }
  .hero .datechip { margin-left: 8px; }
  .legend + p { margin-top: 12px; }

</style>
</Fragment>
<header class="site">
  <div class="nav">
    <a class="brand" href="/"><span class="b1">Blue</span><span class="b2">Yucca</span></a>
    <nav class="nav-links">
      <a href="/business-in-a-box">Business in a Box</a>
      <a href="/examples">Examples</a>
      <a href="/prompt-builder">Prompt Builder</a>
      <a href="/hosting">Hosting Guide</a>
      <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
      <a href="/#about">About</a>
      <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
      <a class="nav-cta" href="/business-in-a-box">Open the box</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">

  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">The checklist</span>
    <h1>Business in a box.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Seven things a small business should own online. For each one: what it is, a free or cheap way to start, a test you can run in about five minutes, and when you might outgrow it. Work down the page and you will see how far along you are. <span class="datechip">Reviewed Oct 2026</span></p>
  </section>

  <div class="current-note reveal">
    <div class="kicker">How to read this page</div>
    <p>Every pick wears one of these labels, so you know how much weight to give it.</p>
    <div class="legend">
      <span class="chip used">Used</span> <span>I use it, or have used it, in a real business.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="legend">
      <span class="chip testing">Testing</span> <span>I am testing it now. Treat it as a candidate.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="legend">
      <span class="chip nottested">Not tested yet</span> <span>It is on my list. I have not tried it.</span>
    </div>
    <p>I also run an exit test on everything: if you cannot take it with you, I flag that as a cost.</p>
    <p>There are no affiliate links on this page. Where I know someone at a company, I say so next to the pick. Prices and plans change, so check the company's own page before you buy.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="current-note reveal" style="background:var(--cream-deep);">
    <div class="kicker">The one cost up front</div>
    <p>This is a free checklist, and most of it can be done for free. The exception is the domain name in item one. It costs money every year, and I would rather tell you that first.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 01 -->
  <section class="item reveal" id="name">
    <div class="item-head"><span class="item-num">01</span><h2>A name you own</h2></div>
    <dl>
      <dt>What it is</dt>
      <dd>Your domain name is your address on the internet. Your website, your email and every link you hand out hang from it. If it is registered in someone else's account, you are renting your own name.</dd>
      <dt>A free or cheap way to start</dt>
      <dd>This one is not free. A .com usually runs somewhere around ten to twenty dollars a year, and prices vary by company and by year. Register it yourself, in your own account, with an email address you read.</dd>
      <dt>Test it yourself</dt>
      <dd><div class="selftest">Log into the account where your domain lives. Check three things: your name or business is listed as the owner, the contact email is one you read, and auto-renew is on with a card that is not about to expire. Then find the transfer lock setting. If you cannot log in at all, someone else controls your name.</div></dd>
      <dt>When you might outgrow it</dt>
      <dd>You do not outgrow owning your name. You may end up with several domains and want all the renewal dates in one place.</dd>
      <dt>My pick</dt>
      <dd><span class="chip cost">No pick yet</span> After twenty years in the domain business I have strong opinions about registrars. I am not naming any yet.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 -->
  <section class="item reveal" id="home">
    <div class="item-head"><span class="item-num">02</span><h2>A home base</h2></div>
    <dl>
      <dt>What it is</dt>
      <dd>A simple website that says who you are, what you do and how to reach you. One page is enough. It is the place all your other tools point to, so it should be a file you can download, not a room in someone else's building.</dd>
      <dt>A free or cheap way to start</dt>
      <dd>Building it with an AI is free, and hosting can be free or a few dollars a month. My <a href="/prompt-builder">prompt builder</a> asks the questions a site has to answer and writes the prompt for you. The <a href="/hosting">hosting guide</a> covers two places to put the finished file.</dd>
      <dt>Test it yourself</dt>
      <dd><div class="selftest">Open your site on your phone using mobile data, not wifi. Does it load in a few seconds? Does the phone number tap to call? Then ask yourself one question: if my host disappeared tomorrow, do I have every file on my own computer?</div></dd>
      <dt>When you might outgrow it</dt>
      <dd>When you need a shopping cart, or hundreds of pages. A real online store with inventory, tax and shipping is the one place where I do not have a simple answer yet. I will say so plainly instead of pretending.</dd>
      <dt>My pick</dt>
      <dd><span class="chip used">Used</span> This site is built this way, and so is the page it started from, a FrontPage 2003 experiment you can <a href="/frontpage/">see here</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- 03 -->
  <section class="item reveal" id="email">
    <div class="item-head"><span class="item-num">03</span><h2>Email on your name</h2></div>
    <dl>
      <dt>What it is</dt>
      <dd>An address like you@yourbusiness.com instead of a free mailbox. It is one of the cheapest ways to look like a real business, and it stays with you if you ever change providers.</dd>
      <dt>A free or cheap way to start</dt>
      <dd>Zoho Mail has a free plan. According to Zoho's own page, it covers up to 5 users with 5 GB of storage each, for one domain. It does not include IMAP or POP, which are the usual ways to connect other mail apps or copy your mail out. Under my exit test, that is a cost to know about.</dd>
      <dt>Test it yourself</dt>
      <dd><div class="selftest">Send a message from your business address to a Gmail account and to one other provider. Does it land in the inbox or in spam? Reply to it and see whether the reply reaches you.</div></dd>
      <dt>When you might outgrow it</dt>
      <dd>When you need your mail in other apps, or more than five people. Paid plans from several companies exist. I have not tested them.</dd>
      <dt>My pick</dt>
      <dd><span class="chip nottested">Not tested yet</span> Zoho Mail is a candidate, and I have not used its free plan myself.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 -->
  <section class="item reveal" id="contact">
    <div class="item-head"><span class="item-num">04</span><h2>A way to be contacted</h2></div>
    <dl>
      <dt>What it is</dt>
      <dd>A form on your site that sends a message to an inbox you read. Without one, you are choosing between posting your email address in public, where spammers collect it, and hoping people find another way.</dd>
      <dt>A free or cheap way to start</dt>
      <dd>Web3Forms. You paste a plain form into your page, and it forwards the messages to you. The free plan keeps submissions for 30 days, and you can export them from the dashboard.</dd>
      <dt>Test it yourself</dt>
      <dd><div class="selftest">Fill in your own form from your phone. Did the message arrive, how fast, and did it land in spam? Try again with a different email address. Then repeat the test every few months, because forms tend to fail quietly.</div></dd>
      <dt>When you might outgrow it</dt>
      <dd>When you want submissions to flow into a spreadsheet or a customer system, or you run many forms. Other form tools exist. I have not tested them.</dd>
      <dt>My pick</dt>
      <dd><span class="chip used">Used</span> Web3Forms runs the contact form on this site.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 -->
  <section class="item reveal" id="paid">
    <div class="item-head"><span class="item-num">05</span><h2>Scheduled and paid</h2></div>
    <dl>
      <dt>What it is</dt>
      <dd>A link people can use to book time with you, and a button or link they can use to pay you. Neither needs a full online store.</dd>
      <dt>A free or cheap way to start</dt>
      <dd>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Booking: Calendly.</strong> It has a free plan, and the link works from any page. <span class="chip nottested">Not tested yet</span> It is my leading candidate, and I have not set up a booking page with it yet.</div>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Paying: a PayPal buy button.</strong> In a PayPal business account you go to Pay &amp; Get Paid, then Create Payment Links and Buttons, set the product and price, and PayPal gives you a snippet to paste into your page. The settings live on PayPal's side, so most product changes do not need new code. PayPal carries a large share of my own store's yearly sales. <span class="chip nottested">Not tested yet</span> I have used PayPal for years, but I have not built this particular button yet.</div>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Paying: a Stripe Payment Link.</strong> The same idea from a different company. <span class="chip nottested">Not tested yet</span> I use Stripe, and I have not tried Payment Links yet.</div>
      </dd>
      <dt>Test it yourself</dt>
      <dd><div class="selftest">Book a slot the way a stranger would, from your phone, with a different email address. Did the confirmation arrive, and did it land on your calendar? For payments, buy your own cheapest item, check the receipt your customer would see, confirm the money reaches your account, and refund yourself.</div></dd>
      <dt>When you might outgrow it</dt>
      <dd>When you have more than a few products and need a cart, shipping and tax. As I said in item two, I do not have a simple answer for that yet.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- 06 -->
  <section class="item reveal" id="list">
    <div class="item-head"><span class="item-num">06</span><h2>A list you can take with you</h2></div>
    <dl>
      <dt>What it is</dt>
      <dd>The names and email addresses of people who said yes to hearing from you. A follower count is a number someone else keeps for you. A list you can export is yours.</dd>
      <dt>A free or cheap way to start</dt>
      <dd>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Brevo.</strong> <span class="chip nottested">Not tested yet</span> I used Mailchimp for years and need to move off it. Brevo is my leading candidate, and I have not used it yet.</div>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Omnisend.</strong> <span class="chip used">Used</span> I used it in my online store. It is built for stores, so it fits best if you sell products online. <em>Disclosure: I know people at Omnisend.</em></div>
      </dd>
      <dt>Test it yourself</dt>
      <dd><div class="selftest">Export your list to a spreadsheet today and open it. Is every address there, with the date and how each person signed up? If you cannot export it, you do not own it.</div></dd>
      <dt>When you might outgrow it</dt>
      <dd>Email tools price by list size, so the bill grows with you. Check the price at your next size before you pick one, not after.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <!-- 07 -->
  <section class="item reveal" id="working">
    <div class="item-head"><span class="item-num">07</span><h2>Know it is working</h2></div>
    <dl>
      <dt>What it is</dt>
      <dd>Three small questions: is anyone visiting, is the site fast, and can people find it in search. You do not need a dashboard full of charts to answer them.</dd>
      <dt>A free or cheap way to start</dt>
      <dd>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Visits: Umami and GoatCounter.</strong> <span class="chip testing">Testing</span> I have run both on this site as tests. Both avoid cookies. Plausible is another candidate, and I have not tested it.</div>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Search: Ahrefs Free.</strong> <span class="chip used">Used</span> The free tier, formerly called Ahrefs Webmaster Tools, covers a site audit and backlink data for sites you can verify you own.</div>
        <div class="pick"><strong>Speed: GTmetrix.</strong> <span class="chip used">Used</span> Free for spot checks. Google's PageSpeed Insights is also free and needs no account.</div>
      </dd>
      <dt>Test it yourself</dt>
      <dd><div class="selftest">Visit your own site from your phone and see whether the visit shows up in your analytics within a minute or two. Run a speed test and read only the top score. Then check whether you can export your numbers.</div></dd>
      <dt>When you might outgrow it</dt>
      <dd>When you want to know which pages bring in customers, not only how many people visited. That is a bigger question than this box answers.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="block reveal">
    <div class="kicker">Done, or not yet</div>
    <h2>Pick one item and run its test.</h2>
    <div class="why">
      <p>Most people find a gap within the first two tests. That is the point of the tests. If you would rather work through the list with someone, that kind of help lives at <a href="https://kakt.ai">kakt.ai</a>. This checklist stays free either way.</p>
      <p>Found a mistake, or a tool I should look at? <a href="/contact">Tell me</a>.</p>
      <p class="fine">Last reviewed: October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

